rocephaly, midface hypoplasia, micrognathia, frontal bossing, and down-slanting palpebral fissures.","All three displayed a severely disturbed ossification of the skull and multiple fractures with prenatal onset."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:25683121:2","pmid":"25683121","label":"Two fetuses","kind":"group","family":"","n_affected":2,"n_families":1,"sex":"","ancestry":"","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"prenatal","age_last":"fetus","phenotypes":[{"text":"severely disturbed ossification of the skull","hpo_label":"Abnormality of skull ossification","hpo_id":"HP:0002703","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"multiple fractures with prenatal onset","hpo_label":"Multiple prenatal fractures","hpo_id":"HP:0005855","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"c.3044C>T (p.Ser1015Phe)","cdna":"c.3044C>T","protein":"p.Ser1015Phe","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"missense","key":"V1"}],"variant_roles":["causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["two fetuses initially suspected to have a severe type of osteogenesis imperfecta","All three displayed a severely disturbed ossification of the skull and multiple fractures with prenatal onset."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:27942778:1","pmid":"27942778","label":"Family 1 proband","kind":"individual","family":"Family 1","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"male","ancestry":"Chinese","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"","age_last":"23 years","phenotypes":[{"text":"recurrent fractures","hpo_label":"Recurrent fractures","hpo_id":"HP:0002757","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"dentinogenesis imperfecta","hpo_label":"Dentinogenesis imperfecta","hpo_id":"HP:0000703","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"unclosed anterior fontanel","hpo_label":"Delayed closure of the anterior fontanelle","hpo_id":"HP:0001476","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"facial dysmorphism","hpo_label":"Abnormal facial shape","hpo_id":"HP:0001999","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"skull deformities","hpo_label":"Abnormal skull morphology","hpo_id":"HP:0000929","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"broad ossification defect in frontoapical area","hpo_label":"Decreased skull ossification","hpo_id":"HP:0004331","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"widened sagittal suture","hpo_label":"Wide cranial sutures","hpo_id":"HP:0010537","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"Wormian bones","hpo_label":"Wormian bones","hpo_id":"HP:0002645","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"c.2723G>A (p. Cys908Tyr)","cdna":"c.2723G>A","protein":"p.Cys908Tyr","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V2"},{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"c.2842T>C (p. Ser948Pro)","cdna":"c.2842T>C","protein":"p.Ser948Pro","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V3"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["In family 1, the proband was a 23-year-old male; he had recurrent fractures and dentinogenesis imperfecta. His anterior fontanel was not closed, and he showed facial dysmorphism.","A computed tomography three-dimensional imaging of the cranium showed skull deformities associated with a broad ossification defect in the frontoapical area, a widened sagittal suture, and Wormian bones.","We identified one novel compound heterozygous missense substitution in the proband in family 1, including c.2723G>A (p. Cys908Tyr) and c.2842T>C (p. Ser948Pro)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:27942778:2","pmid":"27942778","label":"Family 2 proband","kind":"individual","family":"Family 2","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"male","ancestry":"Chinese","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"","age_last":"7 years","phenotypes":[{"text":"recurrent fractures","hpo_label":"Recurrent fractures","hpo_id":"HP:0002757","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"dentinogenesis imperfecta","hpo_label":"Dentinogenesis imperfecta","hpo_id":"HP:0000703","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"unclosed anterior fontanel","hpo_label":"Delayed closure of the anterior fontanelle","hpo_id":"HP:0001476","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"obvious facial dysmorphism","hpo_label":"Abnormal facial shape","hpo_id":"HP:0001999","present":false,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"c.938G>A (p. Arg313His)","cdna":"c.938G>A","protein":"p.Arg313His","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V4"},{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"c.875C>T (p. Pro292Leu)","cdna":"c.875C>T","protein":"p.Pro292Leu","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V5"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["In family 2, the proband was a 7-year-old boy, who also had recurrent fractures and dentinogenesis imperfecta. His anterior fontanel was not closed, and he did not have obvious facial dysmorphism.","In the proband in family 2, we identified another novel compound heterozygous missense substitution, including c.938G>A (p. Arg313His) and c.875C>T (p. Pro292Leu)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:30462379:1","pmid":"30462379","label":"15-year-old Japanese boy","kind":"individual","family":"","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"male","ancestry":"Japanese","consanguinity":"not_stated","onset":"","age_last":"15 years","phenotypes":[{"text":"short stature of the short-trunk type","hpo_label":"Short stature","hpo_id":"HP:0004322","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"short trunk","hpo_label":"Disproportionate short-trunk short stature","hpo_id":"HP:0003521","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"ocular proptosis","hpo_label":"Proptosis","hpo_id":"HP:0000520","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"marked frontal bossing","hpo_label":"Frontal bossing","hpo_id":"HP:0002007","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"midface hypoplasia","hpo_label":"Midface retrusion","hpo_id":"HP:0011800","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"micrognathia","hpo_label":"Micrognathia","hpo_id":"HP:0000347","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"low bone mineral density","hpo_label":"Reduced bone mineral density","hpo_id":"HP:0004349","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"basilar impression","hpo_label":"Basilar impression","hpo_id":"HP:0005758","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false}],"variants":[{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"p.Arg484*","cdna":"","protein":"p.Arg484*","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"nonsense","key":"V6"},{"gene":"SEC24D","as_reported":"p.Arg313His","cdna":"","protein":"p.Arg313His","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"unknown","consequence":"missense","key":"V4"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal"],"segregation":"","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["We describe a 15-year-old Japanese boy with short stature of the short-trunk type and craniofacial abnormalities including ocular proptosis, marked frontal bossing, midface hypoplasia, and micrognathia.","He had low-bone mineral density and basilar impression. Whole exome sequencing analysis identified biallelic variants in SEC24D (p.Arg484* and p.Arg313His) in the patient.","We will report a patient with compound heterozygous variants of SEC24D causing Cole-Carpenter syndrome type 2."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"}],"notes":[{"id":"N:26467156:1","pmid":"26467156","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"Moosa et al. (2016) reported that mutations in the SEC24D gene cause autosomal recessive osteogenesis imperfecta.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["Mutations in SEC24D cause autosomal recessive osteogenesis imperfecta."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:25683121:1","pmid":"25683121","section":"molecular_genetics","statement":"By whole-exome sequencing, Garbes et al. (2015) identified three mutant SEC24D alleles—the truncating c.613C>T (p.Gln205Ter) and the missense c.3044C>T (p.Ser1015Phe, in a cargo-binding pocket) and c.2933A>C (p.Gln978Pro, in the gelsolin-like domain)—in three individuals from two families, each compound heterozygous for two of these alleles. The c.3044C>T allele lay on a 14-Mb founder haplotype shared by all three.","inheritance":"AR","quotes":["we report three mutant alleles in SEC24D, a gene encoding a component of the COPII complex involved in protein export from the ER: the truncating mutation c.613C>T (p.Gln205(∗)) and the missense mutations c.3044C>T (p.Ser1015Phe, located in a cargo-binding pocket) and c.2933A>C (p.Gln978Pro, located in the gelsolin-like domain)","Three individuals from two families affected by a similar skeletal phenotype were each compound heterozygous for two of these mutant alleles, with c.3044C>T being embedded in a 14 Mb founder haplotype shared by all three."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]},{"id":"N:25683121:2","pmid":"25683121","section":"pathogenesis","statement":"Garbes et al. (2015) found by electron and immunofluorescence microscopy that skin fibroblasts from an affected boy showed inefficient ER export of procollagen and dilated ER tubules, reproducing the cellular phenotype of cranio-lentico-sutural dysplasia caused by SEC23A mutations.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["Electron and immunofluorescence microscopy of skin fibroblasts of this individual revealed that ER export of procollagen was inefficient and that ER tubules were dilated, faithfully reproducing the cellular phenotype of individuals with cranio-lentico-sutural dysplasia (CLSD)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0]},{"id":"N:25683121:3","pmid":"25683121","section":"clinical_features","statement":"Garbes et al. (2015) noted that CLSD shows a largely overlapping craniofacial phenotype but lacks generalized bone fragility, and that cataracts were present in the original CLSD family. They stated that the cellular and morphologic phenotypes were concordant with those of Sec24d-deficient medaka (vbi) and zebrafish (bulldog) mutants.","inheritance":"UNKNOWN","quotes":["CLSD is caused by SEC23A mutations and displays a largely overlapping craniofacial phenotype, but it is not characterized by generalized bone fragility and presented with cataracts in the original family described.","The cellular and morphological phenotypes we report are in concordance with the phenotypes described for the Sec24d-deficient fish mutants vbi (medaka) and bulldog (zebrafish)."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0]}],"dropped":{"records":[],"notes":[]},"gene_decisions":{"candidates":["SEC24D"],"confirmed":["SEC24D"],"dropped":[],"not_confirmed":[]},"candidate_inheritance":["AR"]}